<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry I, Duke of Münsterberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1448">1448</a>–<a href="/years/1498">1498</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Henry the Elder of Münsterberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry I, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziebice">Münsterberg</a>, known as the Elder, was a son of the Bohemian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady">George of Poděbrady</a>. He held the Silesian Duchy of Münsterberg and the County of Kladsko (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klodzko">Glatz</a>), which he received in 1472, and founded the Poděbrady line of Silesian dukes. His descendants kept the duchy until the 16th century.</p></div>
